+# NUI v8 — Agent Interoperability & Visual Media Closure
+
+NUI v8 closes two practical gaps that remained after v7: the canonical intelligence could not yet travel cleanly across heterogeneous agent harnesses, and high-ambition UI could still substitute generic geometry for subject-native visual evidence.
+
+## What v8 changes
+
+- **Portable agent surface:** thin discovery bridges for Open Agent Skills-compatible hosts and Claude Code, plus bounded CLI/MCP surfaces. One canonical graph remains the source of truth.
+- **External skill trust firewall:** third-party skills are pinned, hashed, licensed, capability-reviewed and treated as advisory until locally adopted. Transitive scripts/resources are part of the review surface.
+- **Visual media intelligence:** NUI maps semantic media jobs before sourcing, distinguishes useful geometry from shape substitution, and routes to stock/open-culture/public-domain/science/space/geospatial/iconography sources according to domain need.
+- **Asset-level provenance:** a provider or search engine does not certify every asset. Selected assets retain creator, origin, exact rights evidence, attribution, modification/commercial status, caveats and local transformation lineage.
+- **Creative tool orchestration:** Figma/Penpot/Blender/web renderers/motion/data/map/image tools are stage authorities only. They never own product truth, rights truth or completion.
+- **Rendered integration:** media must survive crop, hierarchy, responsive recomposition, loading/failure, performance, accessibility and provenance-to-render checks.
+
+## Shape substitution policy
+
+V8 does not ban rectangles, cards, circles, gradients, diagrams or abstraction. It blocks the more specific failure where low-information geometry consumes high visual salience while impersonating evidence, domain identity or data. A real dependency graph can pass; a decorative network with meaningless edges cannot. A quiet typography-led UI can pass; a glowing orb pretending to be a scientific model cannot.
+
+## Copyright and external-source boundary
+
+V8 defaults to pointers and independently written mechanism summaries. Copying/vendoring requires exact license evidence. Media reuse is verified per asset. Generated media remains subject to product truth, rights, likeness/trademark/privacy and disclosure considerations; “AI-generated” is not a blanket clearance.
+
+## Bounded claim
+
+These mechanisms raise the cost of shallow, generic and provenance-poor UI behavior. They do not guarantee universal beauty, legal clearance, or that a host agent has capabilities it does not expose. Current host/source behavior must be verified when material.
